 "summary_note": "Section 5.34's integrity check, run at probe_candidate_cap=1 so the probed pool holds exactly one candidate and the score cannot decide what gets applied. probe_scoring must then change nothing: the two settings must be bit-identical on the fixed arm, the fused loss, the selected candidates and the booked search FLOPs. A non-identical seed would falsify the claim that the knob changes only the score used to rank a pool whose membership it does not touch - and would mean this study is measuring something else."
